  <div class="dashboard-header">
    <span class="lua-section"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.GetSPMaxMemory(): number`} lang="slua" /></span>
    <span class="lsl-section"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`integer llGetSPMaxMemory();`} lang="lsl" /></span>
  </div>

  <div class="dashboard-body">
    <div class="dash-col">
      <p>  <p>Returns the integer of the most bytes used while <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlScriptProfiler" target="_blank">LlScriptProfiler</a> was last active.</p>
</p>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Categories</div>
      <ul class="meta-list">
        <li>script</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="dash-col">
      <div class="dash-section-title">Tech Specs</div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">Energy</span><span class="tech-val">10</span></div>
      <div class="tech-item"><span class="tech-label">LSO ID</span><span class="tech-val">365</span></div>

      <div class="label-stack">
        <span class="attr-label bg-mandatory">Use Return</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
  <h2>Specification</h2>
  <p>This function&#39;s behavior is dependent upon the VM the script is using. <a href="#Mono" target="_blank">Mono</a> is the new VM, <a href="#LSO" target="_blank">LSO</a> is the old VM. The big difference between between Mono and LSO is that Mono scripts run faster and can utilize four times more memory.</p>
  <h3>Mono</h3>
  <p>During and after a <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/LlScriptProfiler" target="_blank">LlScriptProfiler</a> profiling run, llGetSPMaxMemory will return the most memory used during profiling.</p>
  <h3>LSO</h3>
  <p>This function has no effect for scripts not compiled to Mono. It will always return 16384, the fixed LSO memory size.</p>
  <h2>Examples</h2>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll = llcompat

-- need to run something for the profile to register... 
local function ScriptRotate()
    ll.TargetOmega(vector(0.5, 0.7, 0.2), 0.75, 0.75)
end

local function main()
    ll.SetMemoryLimit(5000)  -- set the memory limit

    -- call up the profiler, execute a method, stop profiler
    ll.ScriptProfiler(PROFILE_SCRIPT_MEMORY)
    ScriptRotate()
    ll.ScriptProfiler(PROFILE_NONE)

    -- display memory usage...
    ll.Say(0, "Memory used: " .. tostring(ll.GetSPMaxMemory()) .. " bytes, total memory: " .. tostring(ll.GetMemoryLimit()) .. " bytes.")
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`// need to run something for the profile to register... 
ScriptRotate()
{
    llTargetOmega(<0.5, 0.7, 0.2>, 0.75, 0.75);
}

default
{
    state_entry()
    {
        llSetMemoryLimit( 5000 ); // set the memory limit
        
        // call up the profiler, execute a method, stop profiler
        llScriptProfiler( PROFILE_SCRIPT_MEMORY );
        ScriptRotate(); 
        llScriptProfiler( PROFILE_NONE );
        
        // display memory usage...
        llSay(0, "Memory used: " + (string)llGetSPMaxMemory() + " bytes, total memory: " + 
            (string)llGetMemoryLimit() + " bytes." );
    }
}

// outputs 
// Object: Memory used: 4448 bytes, total memory: 5000 bytes.`} lang="lsl" /></div>
